From 798ee0be2b53dfc61b65de6d3175813cf39cc582 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 13:10:05 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] CUDA: group the KV-cache K/V set_rows stores into one
 launch

Port of the R9700/HIP track patch 0007 ("CUDA/HIP: group the KV-cache K and V
set_rows stores into one launch", Claude Fable 5), unchanged: shared
ggml-cuda code with no architecture-gated paths. A decode step stores the new
K row and the new V row with two independent set_rows launches; the grouped
kernel routes each block to its segment and keeps every element's source,
cast and destination address, so the result is byte-identical by
construction.

GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_SET_ROWS_GROUP=1 disables the optimization.
---
